\ ***************************************************************************
\ STARGLIDER for the BBC Master - the memory map (docs/plan.md, section 3)
\
\ Each region's guard is its budget, so a part that grows says so when it
\ outgrows it; `make memory` (tools/memmap.py) shows what each holds.
\
\ - zero page: zp.6502; the OS's pages &0400-&0CFF: the workspace (zp.6502);
\   &0D00: the disc reader's NMI routine;
\ - main RAM from &0E00: the code, then the lists and the object table
\   (objects.6502) up to the screen;
\ - shadow RAM's &3000 up to the shadow screen: the erase lists, which only
\   code in HAZEL reads or writes, as only ACCCON's X shows them;
\ - HAZEL: the tables and the code that runs with X set (banks.6502);
\ - sideways RAM: the shapes (bank 4), the world (5: the list phase, the
\   sine table, and the game's logic to come).
\ ***************************************************************************

\ The lists: slot numbers, in the order pushed (world.6502), below the
\ object table.
LISTS = OBJECTS - 3 * OB_SLOTS
SECTION Lists, org = LISTS, guard = OBJECTS, virtual = TRUE
.coarse_slots SKIP OB_SLOTS
.near_slots SKIP OB_SLOTS
.draw_slots SKIP OB_SLOTS
ENDSECTION

\ The top of main RAM's code.
MAIN_TOP = LISTS

\ The erase lists: each screen's lines as the line drawer drew them
\ (x0 word, y0, x1 word, y1), in shadow RAM below the shadow screen.
ERASE_LIST  = &3000
ERASE_ENTRY = 6
ERASE_LINES = (SCREEN - ERASE_LIST) DIV 2 DIV ERASE_ENTRY
ERASE_BYTES = ERASE_LINES * ERASE_ENTRY
ASSERT ERASE_LIST + 2 * ERASE_BYTES <= SCREEN
